#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Result metadata {#result-metadata}"
msgstr "Metadatos del resultado {#result-metadata}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In addition to the execution results, both the `PrimitiveResult` and `SamplerPubResult` objects contain a metadata attribute about the job that was submitted. The metadata containing information for all submitted PUBs (such as the various [runtime options](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options) available) can be found in the `PrimitiveResult.metatada`, while the metadata specific to each PUB is found in `SamplerPubResult.metadata`.\n"
msgstr "Además de los resultados de ejecución, tanto los objetos `PrimitiveResult` como `SamplerPubResult` contienen un atributo de metadatos sobre el job enviado. Los metadatos que contienen información para todos los PUBs enviados (como las diversas [opciones de runtime](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options) disponibles) se pueden encontrar en `PrimitiveResult.metatada`, mientras que los metadatos específicos de cada PUB se encuentran en `SamplerPubResult.metadata`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The client-side Sampler submits its workload as an [Executor](/guides/executor-input-output) job. The metadata of the underlying Executor result, which includes execution timing information called [_execution spans_](#execution-spans), is available under the `\"executor\"` key of `PrimitiveResult.metadata`.\n"
msgstr "El Sampler del lado del cliente envía su carga de trabajo como un job de [Executor](/guides/executor-input-output). Los metadatos del resultado de Executor subyacente, que incluyen información de temporización de ejecución llamada [_spans de ejecución_](#execution-spans), están disponibles bajo la clave `\"executor\"` de `PrimitiveResult.metadata`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"In the metadata field, primitive implementations can return any information about execution that is relevant to them, and there are no key-value pairs that are guaranteed by the base primitive. Thus, the returned metadata might be different in different primitive implementations.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"En el campo de metadatos, las implementaciones primitivas pueden devolver cualquier información sobre la ejecución que sea relevante para ellas, y no hay pares clave-valor garantizados por la primitiva base. Por lo tanto, los metadatos devueltos pueden ser diferentes en diferentes implementaciones de primitivas.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"execution-spans\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"execution-spans\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "View execution spans {#view-execution-spans}"
msgstr "Ver los spans de ejecución {#view-execution-spans}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The client-side Sampler uses Executor to run jobs, which executes its work on the QPU in _chunks_. The timing of each chunk is in `result.metadata[\"executor\"].chunk_timing`, a list of [`ChunkSpan`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/results-chunk-span) objects. Each `ChunkSpan` has `start` and `stop` timestamps and a list of `parts`, where each part gives an item index (`idx_item`) and the number of configurations from that item (`size`) that ran in the chunk.\n"
msgstr "El Sampler del lado del cliente usa Executor para ejecutar jobs, que ejecuta su trabajo en el QPU en _fragmentos_ (chunks). La temporización de cada fragmento está en `result.metadata[\"executor\"].chunk_timing`, una lista de objetos [`ChunkSpan`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/results-chunk-span). Cada `ChunkSpan` tiene marcas de tiempo `start` y `stop` y una lista de `parts`, donde cada parte indica un índice de elemento (`idx_item`) y el número de configuraciones de ese elemento (`size`) que se ejecutaron en el fragmento.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sampler creates one Executor program item per PUB, so `idx_item` is the index of the PUB, in the order the PUBs were given to `run()`. If twirling is enabled, each randomization of each parameter value set counts as a separate configuration.\n"
msgstr "Sampler crea un elemento de programa de Executor por cada PUB, de modo que `idx_item` es el índice del PUB, en el orden en que se pasaron los PUBs a `run()`. Si el twirling está habilitado, cada aleatorización de cada conjunto de valores de parámetros cuenta como una configuración independiente.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To visualize the timings, pass the list to [`draw_chunk_timings`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/visualization-draw-chunk-timings), as shown in the following example.\n"
msgstr "Para visualizar las temporizaciones, pasa la lista a [`draw_chunk_timings`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/visualization-draw-chunk-timings), como se muestra en el siguiente ejemplo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To learn what the chunk timestamps mean, how to read the plot, and why gaps can appear between chunks, see [View execution spans](/guides/executor-input-output#execution-spans) in the Executor inputs and outputs guide.\n"
msgstr "Para saber qué significan las marcas de tiempo de los fragmentos, cómo leer el gráfico y por qué pueden aparecer huecos entre fragmentos, consulta [Ver spans de ejecución](/guides/executor-input-output#execution-spans) en la guía de entradas y salidas de Executor.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"legacy-execution-spans\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"legacy-execution-spans\"></span>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Execution spans in the legacy Sampler {#execution-spans-in-the-legacy-sampler}"
msgstr "Spans de ejecución en el Sampler heredado {#execution-spans-in-the-legacy-sampler}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As of `qiskit-ibm-runtime` v0.50.0, the legacy server-side Sampler is deprecated. The client-side Sampler does not return `ExecutionSpans` objects; use the [chunk timing](#execution-spans) described previously instead. See [Migrate to client-side primitives](/guides/migrate-to-client-side-primitives) for instructions to migrate.\n"
msgstr "A partir de `qiskit-ibm-runtime` v0.50.0, el Sampler heredado del lado del servidor está obsoleto. El Sampler del lado del cliente no devuelve objetos `ExecutionSpans`; usa en su lugar la [temporización de fragmentos](#execution-spans) descrita anteriormente. Consulta [Migrar a primitivas del lado del cliente](/guides/migrate-to-client-side-primitives) para ver las instrucciones de migración.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    <Accordion>\n"
"    <AccordionItem title=\"**Click to learn more.**\">\n"
"    The results of jobs from the legacy server-side [`Sampler`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/sampler-v2) contain execution timing information in `result.metadata[\"execution\"][\"execution_spans\"]`, in the form of an [`ExecutionSpans`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/execution-span-execution-spans) object. This object is a list-like container of [`ExecutionSpan`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/execution-span-execution-span) objects, each of which indicates a start time, a stop time, and a specification of which shots were collected in the span.\n"
msgstr ""
"    <Accordion>\n"
"    <AccordionItem title=\"**Haz clic para saber más.**\">\n"
"    Los resultados de los jobs del [`Sampler`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/sampler-v2) heredado del lado del servidor contienen información de temporización de ejecución en `result.metadata[\"execution\"][\"execution_spans\"]`, en forma de un objeto [`ExecutionSpans`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/execution-span-execution-spans). Este objeto es un contenedor similar a una lista de objetos [`ExecutionSpan`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/execution-span-execution-span), cada uno de los cuales indica una hora de inicio, una hora de fin y una especificación de qué shots se recopilaron en el span.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "    An execution span specifies which data was executed during its window by providing an [`ExecutionSpan.mask`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/execution-span-execution-span#mask) method. This method, given any PUB index, returns a boolean mask that is `True` for all shots executed during its window. If, for example, a PUB has shape `(2, 3)` and was run with four shots, then the mask's shape is `(2, 3, 4)`. See the [execution_span](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/execution-span) API page for full details.\n"
msgstr "    Un span de ejecución especifica qué datos se ejecutaron durante su ventana proporcionando un método [`ExecutionSpan.mask`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/execution-span-execution-span#mask). Este método, dado cualquier índice de PUB, devuelve una máscara booleana que es `True` para todos los shots ejecutados durante su ventana. Si, por ejemplo, un PUB tiene forma `(2, 3)` y se ejecutó con cuatro shots, entonces la forma de la máscara es `(2, 3, 4)`. Consulta la página API de [execution_span](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/execution-span) para obtener todos los detalles.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python noexec\n"
"    from qiskit.primitives import BitArray\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "    spans = result.metadata[\"execution\"][\"execution_spans\"]\n"
msgstr "    spans = result.metadata[\"execution\"][\"execution_spans\"]\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    # Get the mask of the 1st PUB for the 0th span.\n"
"    mask = spans[0].mask(0)\n"
msgstr ""
"    # Obtén la máscara del 1.er PUB para el span 0.\n"
"    mask = spans[0].mask(0)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    # Create a new bit array containing only the PUB-0 data collected during this span.\n"
"    bits = result[0].data.meas\n"
"    filtered_data = BitArray(bits.array[mask], bits.num_bits)\n"
msgstr ""
"    # Crea un nuevo bit array que contenga solo los datos del PUB 0 recopilados durante este span.\n"
"    bits = result[0].data.meas\n"
"    filtered_data = BitArray(bits.array[mask], bits.num_bits)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    # Take the subset of spans that reference data in PUBs 0 or 2\n"
"    spans.filter_by_pub([0, 2])\n"
msgstr ""
"    # Toma el subconjunto de spans que hacen referencia a datos de los PUBs 0 o 2\n"
"    spans.filter_by_pub([0, 2])\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    # View global information about the collection of execution spans\n"
"    print(\"Number of execution spans:\", len(spans))\n"
"    print(\"  Start of the first span:\", spans.start)\n"
"    print(\"     End of the last span:\", spans.stop)\n"
"    print(\"       Total duration (s):\", spans.duration)\n"
"    ```\n"
msgstr ""
"    # Consulta la información global de la colección de spans de ejecución\n"
"    print(\"Number of execution spans:\", len(spans))\n"
"    print(\"  Start of the first span:\", spans.start)\n"
"    print(\"     End of the last span:\", spans.stop)\n"
"    print(\"       Total duration (s):\", spans.duration)\n"
"    ```\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "    To visualize legacy execution spans, use the [`draw_execution_spans`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/visualization-draw-execution-spans) function.\n"
msgstr "    Para visualizar los spans de ejecución heredados, usa la función [`draw_execution_spans`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/visualization-draw-execution-spans).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    It is possible for time windows specified by distinct execution spans to overlap. This is not because a QPU was performing multiple executions simultaneously, but is instead an artifact of certain classical processing that might happen concurrently with quantum execution. The guarantee is that the referenced data definitely occurred in the reported execution span, but not necessarily that the limits of the time window are as tight as possible.\n"
"  </AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
msgstr ""
"    Es posible que las ventanas de tiempo especificadas por distintos spans de ejecución se superpongan. Esto no se debe a que un QPU esté realizando múltiples ejecuciones simultáneamente, sino que es un artefacto de cierto procesamiento clásico que puede ocurrir al mismo tiempo que la ejecución cuántica. La garantía es que los datos referenciados ocurrieron con certeza en el span de ejecución indicado, pero no necesariamente que los límites de la ventana de tiempo sean lo más ajustados posible.\n"
"  </AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
